course: dictionary
lesson: 5490
title: Laugh: with or at
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Lily calms Maddie down, and Maddie makes Lily laugh.» Here laugh is a verb. It means to make sounds with your voice because you think something is funny or you feel happy. The sentence shows that Maddie's actions made Lily happy.
explain: Laugh can also be a noun: «That was a good laugh.» Here a laugh is something fun, or the sound of laughing. You can also say have a laugh, burst out laughing, or laugh out loud.
explain: Laughing with someone is friendly, but laughing at someone means making fun of them, and that can hurt. The text says «never laughing at someone's food, clothes or customs.» Look at the words around laugh to tell which one the writer means.
fact: Laugh is a verb and a noun: you can laugh, or you can have a laugh.
fact: The verb changes its form: laughs (one person, now), laughed (in the past), and laughing (happening now).
fact: «Laugh at» means to make fun of someone, and it can be unkind. «Laugh with» means you are both enjoying something together.
fact: «Laughing stock» means someone everybody laughs at, usually because of a silly mistake.
fact: «Laugh at the advert's trick, not at the person who believed it» means the trick is funny, but the person who was fooled should not be mocked.
exercise: «Lily calms Maddie down, and Maddie makes Lily laugh.» What does laugh mean here? | Sing a long song | Cry loudly | *Make sounds with your voice because something is funny or you feel happy | Stop moving
exercise: Respect means «never laughing at someone's food, clothes or customs.» What does laughing at someone mean? | To hug someone warmly | *To make fun of someone | To say hello politely | To laugh with a friend about a joke
exercise: «That was a good laugh.» Here, what is a laugh? | A kind of cake | A short walk | *Something fun, or the sound of laughing | A question
test: Yesterday Ava ___ at the funny film. | laughs | laugh | *laughed | laughing
test: Which sentence shows a kind kind of laughing? | Ben laughed at Sara when she tripped and fell over | *Ben and Sara laughed together about the silly joke | Ben laughed at the cloud | Ben laughed at his own shoes
exam: What does «burst out laughing» mean? | *Suddenly start laughing loudly | Run out of the room | Cry and shout | Stop talking and sit down
